# A quad whose faces use negative, relative indices.
#
# `f -4 -3 -2 -1` resolves against the vertex count as it stands at that point in
# the file, which is four, so the corners are 0, 1, 2, 3. The in-order face
# statement right after it indexes the same vertices the same way, so a correct
# implementation collapses the two duplicate triangles in distinct() and produces
# exactly one triangle.
#
# This is the case that would catch an implementation resolving relative indices
# against the final vertex count instead of the running one.

v -1.0 0.0 -1.0
v  1.0 0.0 -1.0
v  1.0 0.0  1.0
v -1.0 0.0  1.0

usemtl ground

f -4 -3 -2 -1
f 1 2 3 4
